# Local backend refresh

After finishing backend work in **ord-api**, restart or reset the local JVM app when changes require it:

```bash
# from ord-ops (recommended)
make api-restart

# or from ord-api
make restart
```

- **Fast dev** — `spring-boot:run` with tests fully skipped (`-Dmaven.test.skip=true`). Broken tests do not block local runs.
- **DB stays in Docker** — only the Spring Boot process restarts on `make restart`.
- **First-time start:** `make api-run` (ord-ops) or `make run` (ord-api).
- **After Flyway migration:** `make db-wipe` then `make run`.
- **Full dev stack wipe:** `ord-ops make dev-wipe` (rebuilds docker stack + frontend).

## Tests and OpenAPI

```bash
make test        # controller tests with AI stubs (CI default)
make test-live   # same suite with real OpenAI (.env.test)
make openapi     # after DTO changes — export spec, sync types on frontend
```

## E2E stack

Start the Playwright backend only from **ord-ops**: `make playwright-up`. Do not use docker-e2e targets from ord-api.
